# Selected-method measurement qualification tools

These development tools compare the three pinned geometry methods with the actual
Rust measurement API. They do not ship application behavior. The supplied-fact
oracle, real DOM developer fixture, and complete application are separate scopes.
Node's built-in TypeScript erasure preserves the selected original method bodies;
source hashes and the permitted export/class wrapper adaptation are recorded.

The bridge requires explicit node, border and observation objects. An absent label
is `observation.bounds: null`; omitted bounds or a malformed container is an input
error. Float values use 16 lowercase hexadecimal bits, including signed zero.
The caller owns input memory; `apply` returns a separate output allocation. The
transport reacquires the memory buffer after calls and frees each allocation once.
Unsafe exports require valid live pointer/length pairs and are not a hostile-WASM
memory API. The 1-MiB developer input quota is not a whole-application memory bound.

Use `run_browser.py --build BUILD_CAPTURE --methods ORIGINAL_METHODS_JS --node NODE
--browser CHROMIUM --playwright PLAYWRIGHT_PACKAGE --libraries SHARED_LIBRARY_DIR
--out FRESH_WORKSPACE_OUTPUT`. Each path is explicit; `--out` must be fresh and on
`/workspace`. The build capture must contain the reviewed WASM and passing receipt;
the methods directory must retain `source-binding.json`. Inputs are checked before
and after, including build/source closure, tool code, SDK and shared libraries.
The runner takes the shared runtime lock, serves only owned files on loopback,
retains failures, limits the child lifetime, and closes its server and browser.

For the genuine old-fixture recovery counterexample, use the new runner with
`--assets /workspace/build/builderbob/syson-batch21-20261029/measurement-tools-before-review`
and `--recovery-only`. It injects a one-shot exception at the actual WASM transport
call. The old async event path rejects and remains busy; retain that failed run.
Repeat with current assets and a different fresh output: controls, text and focus
must survive the exception, and the next measurement must succeed. Full mode adds
two warmups/seven measurements at each viewport plus stale/missing/retention checks.

Separately run malformed-envelope probes against retained old and rebuilt bridges:
remove `observation`, remove `bounds`, or replace/remove `node.border`. The old
bridge silently defaulted these cases; the repaired bridge must return an input
error with no size or host calls. Preserve valid `bounds: null` and the 35-case
numeric/refusal replay as controls. Root owns these executions and their receipts.

Screenshots use synthetic fixture styles, not full native rendering. Note has no
synthetic padding; both overflow axes are reported against actual rendered boxes.
Missing CJK/emoji fonts and complete application/browser/device/accessibility
acceptance remain open even when original/Rust formula bits agree. Phase timings
include the named DOM, source-method and JSON/WASM bridge work; they do not establish
pure Rust API speed, native application speed or supported product capacity.
